<!-- ============================================================
     Loan Defaulters Analysis — Tableau Workbook
     Author   : Steja28
     Version  : Tableau Desktop 2023.x
     Created  : 2026
     ============================================================

     PLACEHOLDER FILE — Replace this with the actual exported .twb
     from Tableau Desktop using:
         File → Export As Version → Save as .twb (XML)

     This file is tracked in Git for diff-friendly version control.
     The packaged .twbx (with embedded data) is excluded via .gitignore.

     DATA SOURCES:
       - Loan_default.xlsx        (Transaction-level, joined on LoanID)
       - Borrower_Demographics.xlsx (Demographic attributes, joined on LoanID)

     DASHBOARDS:
       1. Story   : Loan Defaulters Analysis (4 story points)
       2. Dashboard: Loan Vs Income Analysis
       3. Dashboard: Defaults Vs Credit Score Analysis

     CALCULATED FIELDS:
       - Age Groups Bin    : IF [Age] < 28 THEN "18-27" ...
       - Credit Score Range: INT([CreditScore] / 25) * 25
       - Loan_default Count: COUNT([Loan_default])

     KEY FINDINGS:
       - Highest-risk: Age 28-37, married, part-time, credit 850 → 12.05% auto default
       - Business risk: Age 28-37, credit 300, single → 10.45% default
       - Safest: Age 48-57, credit 500-550, education loans
       - Part-time 28-37 → 8.54% default rate (highest by employment)

     HOW TO INSPECT:
       grep -o '<worksheet name="[^"]*"' Loan_Analysis.twb
       grep -A3 '<calculation' Loan_Analysis.twb | head -60

     ============================================================ -->

